---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ImpactStats from '../components/ImpactStats.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const consult = 'https://cal.com/jessica-metayer-1kh8sr/organizational-consultation';
const checklist = base + '/#checklist';
const formats = [
  { name: 'Single workshop or team circle', what: '90 minutes to 3 hours. A strong first step for a staff meeting, offsite, or retreat day.', price: '$1,000' },
  { name: 'Workshop series', what: '4 sessions, weekly or biweekly, so new practices have time to take root between sessions.', price: '$3,000' },
  { name: 'Half-day or full-day immersion', what: 'A deeper, in-person reset for your team, with movement, reflection, and small-group practice.', price: '$3,500' },
  { name: 'Hybrid cohort', what: '8 to 12 weeks of live sessions, practice between sessions, and peer pods for lasting change.', price: '$5,000' },
  { name: 'Executive advisory', what: '3 to 6 months of leadership coaching and culture strategy for executive teams.', price: '$15,000' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="For Organizations | Jess Breathe & Flow"
  description="Trauma-informed workshops, healing circles, and leadership programs that help teams build real trust and sustain the work together. Serving schools, nonprofits, companies, and city programs."
  path="/organizations"
  ctaText="Request a Consultation"
  ctaHref={consult}
>
<style>
  .wrap.center > p { margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .format-list { display: grid; gap: 16px; margin: 40px auto 16px; max-width: 880px; }
  .format-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 2fr auto; gap: 24px; align-items: center; background: var(--ivory); border: 1px solid rgba(93,132,145,0.2); border-radius: 6px; padding: 22px 28px; text-align: left; }
  .format-row h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0; color: var(--slate, #5D8491); }
  .format-row p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .format-price { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--clay, #A36F35); white-space: nowrap; text-align: right; }
  .format-price small { display: block; font-family: var(--font-body, 'Lato', sans-serif); font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--stone, #6b6b6b); }
  .format-note { font-size: 0.9rem; opacity: 0.85; }
  .topic-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 28px; margin: 40px 0; text-align: left; }
  .topic-grid h3 { color: var(--clay, #A36F35); font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .topic-grid p { font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .who-list { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 10px 14px; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 24px auto 0; max-width: 820px; }
  .who-list li { border: 1px solid rgba(93,132,145,0.35); border-radius: 999px; padding: 8px 18px; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .success-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 28px; margin: 40px 0 24px; text-align: left; }
  .success-grid h3 { color: var(--clay, #A36F35); font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .from-to { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.35rem; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 760px; margin: 24px auto 0; }
  .case-study { background: var(--ivory); border-radius: 6px; padding: 36px 40px; text-align: left; max-width: 880px; margin: 32px auto 0; }
  .case-study h3 { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .case-study .case-sub { font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .case-study h4 { font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--clay, #A36F35); margin: 20px 0 6px; }
  .case-study blockquote { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.15rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--clay, #A36F35); padding-left: 18px; margin: 24px 0 6px; }
  .research-note { font-size: 0.82rem; opacity: 0.8; margin-top: 12px; }
  .stakes-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; max-width: 720px; margin: 28px auto 0; text-align: left; }
  .stakes-list li { padding: 14px 0 14px 28px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,253,234,0.2); position: relative; }
  .stakes-list li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 4px; top: 24px; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--clay, #A36F35); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .format-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; padding: 20px; }
    .format-price { text-align: left; }
    .topic-grid, .success-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .case-study { padding: 28px 22px; }
  }
</style>

<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">For Organizations</p>
    <h1>Build a team that trusts each other enough to <span class="annotate annotate-underline">sustain the work<svg viewBox="0 0 180 20" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="M4 11 Q 45 3, 90 10 T 176 9"/></svg></span>.</h1>
    <p class="subhead">Many leaders care deeply about their people and still watch them burn out. We design trauma-informed workshops, healing circles, and leadership programs that build real trust, in the body and in relationship.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a href={consult} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">Request a Consultation</a>
      <a href={checklist} class="btn btn-secondary">Take the Quiet Weight Checklist</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight tint-mist">
  <div class="wrap center">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--inner-light);">Trusted by</p>
    <h2 style="color: var(--ivory);">Workday &middot; International Justice Mission &middot; City of Lyon &middot; City of Boston Age Strong</h2>
  </div>
</section>

<ImpactStats />

<section class="curved-section">
  <div class="wrap center">
    <h2>You already know your people are carrying more than they show.</h2>
    <p class="subhead mx-auto">And you don't know how to reach them without it feeling performative.</p>
    <ul class="stakes-list">
      <li>Good people keep quietly burning out, and the ones you most want to keep are the first to leave.</li>
      <li>The tension no one names keeps shaping every meeting, every decision, and every handoff.</li>
      <li>Your next wellness budget goes to another training people politely sit through and forget by Friday.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="pull-quote">People shouldn't have to leave parts of themselves at the door to do good work.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="wrap center">
    <p class="eyebrow">Who we work with</p>
    <h2>Built for the people responsible for other people.</h2>
    <ul class="who-list">
      <li>Schools &amp; educators</li>
      <li>Nonprofits</li>
      <li>Companies</li>
      <li>City &amp; community programs</li>
      <li>Leadership teams &amp; retreats</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tint-ivory" style="background: var(--inner-light);">
  <div class="wrap center">
    <p class="eyebrow">What we explore together</p>
    <h2>Every engagement is built from what your team needs.</h2>
    <div class="topic-grid">
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Trauma-Informed Learning</h3>
        <p>Understand how stress and trauma show up at work, and how to respond with repair instead of reaction.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Belonging &amp; Connection</h3>
        <p>Build trust that isn't performative, through guided practice, story, and shared presence.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Self As Instrument</h3>
        <p>Leadership grounded in the body. Five practices: Awareness, Alignment, Regulation, Resonance, and Responsibility.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Healing Circles for Teams</h3>
        <p>A held space for your people to set down what they've been carrying, together.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Sound &amp; Stillness</h3>
        <p>Guided sound healing and meditation for deep, collective rest.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Movement</h3>
        <p>On-site or virtual yoga and breathwork for every body and every experience level.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap center">
    <p class="eyebrow">Ways to work together</p>
    <h2>Start with one session, or build something that lasts.</h2>
    <div class="format-list">
      {formats.map((f) => (
        <div class="format-row reveal">
          <h3>{f.name}</h3>
          <p>{f.what}</p>
          <p class="format-price"><small>Starting at</small>{f.price}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="format-note">Every engagement is tailored. Final pricing depends on group size, format, and location.</p>
    <div class="center-actions">
      <a href={consult} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">Request a Consultation</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="about-preview">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your guide</p>
      <h2>We know what it's like to care deeply and still watch people burn out.</h2>
      <p>We've sat in the trainings that changed nothing. Jess Breathe &amp; Flow was built to do the part those trainings skip: helping people feel safe enough to show up honestly, together.</p>
      <p>Jessica Metayer holds an MS in Organization Development from Pepperdine Graziadio Business School. Her graduate research with Black executive leaders explored the hidden labor of sustaining yourself under pressure inside organizations. She brings 5 years of facilitating healing circles, 500-hour advanced yoga training, and practice in breathwork, sound healing, and Reiki.</p>
      <p>Her organization development work reaches across cultures: lead facilitator of an Appreciative Inquiry large-group workshop for Workday in Costa Rica, co-designer of a three-day culture change engagement for BCon's human capital team in Japan, and lead facilitator for the City of Lyon Ecological Transition Team in France.</p>
      <p class="credentials-line">MS, Organization Development, Pepperdine | Trauma-Informed Practice | 500-Hour Advanced-Trained Yoga Teacher | GPS Trained Facilitator</p>
      <p class="research-note">Jessica's research shapes how these programs are designed. It did not evaluate JBAF programs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="split-media"><img src={base + "/images/org-trauma-informed-learning.jpg"} alt="Jessica facilitating a leadership workshop circle discussion" loading="lazy"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap center mx-auto" style="max-width: 720px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h2>Three steps to something your team will actually use.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item reveal">
        <p class="step-number">01</p>
        <h3>Request a consultation</h3>
        <p>A 30-minute call about your people, your goals, and what's already been tried.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-item reveal">
        <p class="step-number">02</p>
        <h3>We design it together</h3>
        <p>A tailored proposal with topic, format, and price, built around your team, not a template.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-item reveal">
        <p class="step-number">03</p>
        <h3>Your team experiences it, and we follow up</h3>
        <p>Jessica leads every session personally, then shares integration resources and a short debrief on what surfaced and what comes next.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight tint-inner-light">
  <div class="wrap center mx-auto" style="max-width: 640px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">What you can count on</p>
    <h2>How we hold this space, for organizations</h2>
    <ul class="agreement-list" style="text-align: left; display: inline-grid;">
      <li>Built around your goals, not a template</li>
      <li>What your team shares stays confidential</li>
      <li>Jessica leads personally, every time</li>
      <li>Trauma-informed, with participation always by choice</li>
      <li>Designed for lasting change, not a one-time event</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap center">
    <p class="eyebrow">What changes</p>
    <h2>Trust you can feel in the room.</h2>
    <div class="success-grid">
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Your team has</h3>
        <p>Shared language for stress, conflict, and repair. Simple regulation practices people actually use.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>It feels like</h3>
        <p>Meetings where people say the real thing. Less bracing, more breathing. Leaders who can hold hard moments.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>A Tuesday looks like</h3>
        <p>Someone names the tension, and it gets handled instead of avoided. People stay.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="from-to">From a group of people holding it together separately, to a team that trusts each other enough to sustain the work together.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tint-mist">
  <div class="wrap center">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--inner-light);">Case studies</p>
    <h2 style="color: var(--ivory);">Proof from the rooms we've held</h2>
    <div class="case-study">
      <h3>City of Boston Age Strong Commission</h3>
      <p class="case-sub">In partnership with ThriveHub</p>
      <h4>The need</h4>
      <p>Boston's older adults reflect the city's diversity, but the wellness spaces available to them often don't. Age Strong wanted practitioners who look like the people they serve, so culturally relevant wellness could reach residents who have long been excluded from it.</p>
      <h4>What we delivered</h4>
      <p>Chair yoga, breathwork, mobility, strength building, and meditation, in 4-week series of 1-hour sessions. Every class offers options for each movement, invites breaks, and asks people to say when something doesn't feel right, so participants build awareness of their own bodies as they move.</p>
      <h4>What happened</h4>
      <p>Since January 2026, Jessica has taught 27 sessions at the Veronica B. Smith Senior Center, regularly with 22 or more participants. Many return week after week, and attendance rises when participants learn she's teaching. In fall 2026, the work expanded to three new series in Copley, Holland, and Jamaica Plain.</p>
      <blockquote>"I have had trouble sleeping for a very long time. Since taking your classes, I am able to relax and sleep at night."</blockquote>
      <p style="font-size: 0.9rem;">Participant, Veronica B. Smith Senior Center</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-study">
      <h3>School Wellness Club Pilot</h3>
      <p class="case-sub">A 10-week pilot at a Boston Public Schools elementary school, spring 2026</p>
      <h4>The need</h4>
      <p>Students need spaces within the school day where they can slow down, express themselves, build healthy relationships, and practice ways to respond to difficult emotions. The pilot was designed as a club, not a clinical intervention, so it felt low pressure and centered on curiosity and community.</p>
      <h4>What we delivered</h4>
      <p>A 10-session wellness club blending yoga, mindfulness, emotional check-ins, reflection, play, and creative choice like clay, drawing, and origami. Lessons drew on age-appropriate themes such as kindness, contentment, and self-awareness, and the club adapted to what students showed they needed.</p>
      <h4>What happened</h4>
      <p>Students grew closer and the club became a place they wanted to return to. Students outside the group heard about it and asked to join. On the closing survey, 3 of 3 respondents said they were happy to be in the group, learned a new activity, and believed their friends would like it.</p>
      <blockquote>"Keep on going."</blockquote>
      <p style="font-size: 0.9rem;">Student, closing survey</p>
      <p class="research-note">A small pilot with 3 survey respondents, shared as early evidence. The next cycle adds pre and post measures.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight" id="consult">
  <div class="wrap center mx-auto" style="max-width: 640px;">
    <h2>Let's build something that lasts for your people.</h2>
    <p class="subhead mx-auto">Book a free 30-minute consultation. We'll talk about your team, your goals, and what's already been tried.</p>
    <div class="center-actions">
      <a href={consult} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">Request a Consultation</a>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top: 16px; font-size: 0.9rem;">Not ready yet? <a href={checklist}>Take the Quiet Weight Checklist</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
